From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 55/59] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi-qp: fresh EDID on each probe,
 resend ELD on change

get_modes reused connector->edid_blob_ptr whenever it was set, so a
connected sink kept its first EDID until a disconnected detect cleared
the property. On 6.1 a debugfs edid_override "reset" cleared the
property (drm_edid_override_reset -> drm_connector_update_edid_property
NULL); since 6.3 it only frees connector->edid_override, so neither a
new drm.edid_firmware value, a debugfs override nor "reset" followed by
a status "detect" reaches the connector on 6.12.

Read the EDID through drm_edid_read_ddc() on every probe (override,
firmware parameter, then DDC, as mainline dw-hdmi does). Keep the last
EDID only when that read fails on a re-probe.

hdmi-codec copies the ELD in its plugged callback, which detect calls
before get_modes has updated connector->eld, so the ALSA ELD control
stayed one probe behind after a hotplug. Call the plugged callback
again when the ELD changed.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
index f0bca068a..058497637 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
@@ -3236,6 +3236,8 @@ static int dw_hdmi_connector_get_modes(struct drm_connector *connector)
 	struct drm_display_info *info = &connector->display_info;
 	void *data = hdmi->plat_data->phy_data;
 	struct drm_property_blob *edid_blob_ptr = connector->edid_blob_ptr;
+	u8 old_eld[MAX_ELD_BYTES];
+	bool eld_changed;
 	int i, ret = 0;
 	int ext_block_num;
 
@@ -3283,10 +3285,14 @@ static int dw_hdmi_connector_get_modes(struct drm_connector *connector)
 	memset(metedata, 0, sizeof(*metedata));
 	memset(hdmi->vendor_info, 0, VENDOR_INFO_LEN);
 
-	if (edid_blob_ptr && edid_blob_ptr->length)
+	/* fresh read each probe: debugfs override, drm.edid_firmware and a new sink apply */
+	drm_edid = drm_edid_read_ddc(connector, hdmi->ddc);
+	/* DDC miss on a re-probe: keep last EDID of this connection */
+	if (!drm_edid && edid_blob_ptr && edid_blob_ptr->length)
 		drm_edid = drm_edid_alloc(edid_blob_ptr->data, edid_blob_ptr->length);
-	else
-		drm_edid = drm_edid_read_ddc(connector, hdmi->ddc);
+	mutex_lock(&connector->eld_mutex);
+	memcpy(old_eld, connector->eld, MAX_ELD_BYTES);
+	mutex_unlock(&connector->eld_mutex);
 
 	if (drm_edid)
 		edid = drm_edid_raw(drm_edid);
@@ -3300,6 +3306,12 @@ static int dw_hdmi_connector_get_modes(struct drm_connector *connector)
 		ret = drm_edid_connector_update(connector, drm_edid);
 		if (!ret)
 			ret = drm_edid_connector_add_modes(connector);
+		/* hdmi-codec caches ELD at plug-in, before this update: resend on change */
+		mutex_lock(&connector->eld_mutex);
+		eld_changed = memcmp(old_eld, connector->eld, MAX_ELD_BYTES);
+		mutex_unlock(&connector->eld_mutex);
+		if (eld_changed)
+			handle_plugged_change(hdmi, true);
 
 		edid_blob_ptr = connector->edid_blob_ptr;
 		ext_block_num = edid_blob_ptr->length / HDMI_EDID_BLOCK_LEN - 1;
